## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to craft a DP with a value that mixes sum and max, requiring non-overlapping window management and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Non-overlapping subarrays
- Value function: sum minus max
- DP with reconstruction
- Time/space trade-offs through precomputation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Core DP sketch
let val = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(n+1).fill(0));
for (let i=1;i<=n;i++){
  let maxv = -Infinity, s=0;
  for (let j=i;j>=1;j--){
    s += arr[j];
    maxv = Math.max(maxv, arr[j]);
    val[j][i] = s - maxv;
  }
}
let dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
let par = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
dp[0][0] = 0;
for (let i=1;i<=n;i++){
  for (let t=1;t<=k;t++){
    dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t];
    for (let j=1;j<=i;j++){
      if (dp[j-1][t-1] + val[j][i] > dp[i][t]){
        dp[i][t] = dp[j-1][t-1] + val[j][i];
        par[i][t] = j;
      }
    }
  }
}
```

